  "body": {
    "id": "lem:identification-fwl",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_{N,T,\\mathbf n}(\\lambda)\\), \\[\\tau_n(z_0)=\\sum_{s=1}^{S}\\pi_s\\{\\mathbb E_P[\\bar B_s^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\mid z_0,E_0]-m_s(z_{0s})\\}.\\] On every realized sample for which all selected Gram matrices pass and the foldwise minimizers exist, profiling the event coefficient gives \\(\\widehat\\theta_{sk}=\\bar B_s^{\\mathrm{obs}}-e_0^{\\top}\\widehat\\gamma_{sk}\\); the event term then has no \\(\\gamma\\)-dependent component, the fitted \\(\\widehat\\gamma_{sk}\\) is exactly the historical local-polynomial fit in \\texttt{def:feasible-estimator}, and \\(\\theta_{\\mathrm{FWL}}=\\widehat\\tau\\) exactly.",
    "free_symbols": [
